{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function wasCancelRequested(runs, runId): Promise<boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L71","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:71"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether an explicit cancel has been recorded for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Answers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" rather than throwing when the store cannot be read. Callers\nare middleware abort hooks, which are already on a teardown path, and a\nstore failure there must not replace the caller's own reason for tearing\ndown with a store error. The cost of a false negative is that a cancel\ndegrades into a detach — the run record gains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandboxKey"},{"type":"text","value":"\ninstead of transitioning to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'aborted'"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reapDetachedRuns"},{"type":"text","value":" recovers that run once the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedRunTtlMs"},{"type":"text","value":" the\napplication passes to that sweep has elapsed — nothing derives it from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":", which has no TTL option — so the cost is a delayed teardown\nrather than a lost one, provided the application actually schedules the\nsweep, which is its job and not the framework's. Still strictly better than\nfailing the teardown."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RunStore.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"runs","text":"runs","level":3},{"id":"runid","text":"runId","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction wasCancelRequested(runs, runId): Promise<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:71](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L71)\n\nWhether an explicit cancel has been recorded for `runId`.\n\nAnswers `false` rather than throwing when the store cannot be read. Callers\nare middleware abort hooks, which are already on a teardown path, and a\nstore failure there must not replace the caller's own reason for tearing\ndown with a store error. The cost of a false negative is that a cancel\ndegrades into a detach — the run record gains `detachedSince`/`sandboxKey`\ninstead of transitioning to `'aborted'`. `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s\n`reapDetachedRuns` recovers that run once the `detachedRunTtlMs` the\napplication passes to that sweep has elapsed — nothing derives it from\n`withSandbox`, which has no TTL option — so the cost is a delayed teardown\nrather than a lost one, provided the application actually schedules the\nsweep, which is its job and not the framework's. Still strictly better than\nfailing the teardown.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### runs\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n### runId\n\n`string`\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`boolean`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: wasCancelRequested\ntitle: wasCancelRequested\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction wasCancelRequested(runs, runId): Promise<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts:71](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/cancel.ts#L71)\n\nWhether an explicit cancel has been recorded for `runId`.\n\nAnswers `false` rather than throwing when the store cannot be read. Callers\nare middleware abort hooks, which are already on a teardown path, and a\nstore failure there must not replace the caller's own reason for tearing\ndown with a store error. The cost of a false negative is that a cancel\ndegrades into a detach — the run record gains `detachedSince`/`sandboxKey`\ninstead of transitioning to `'aborted'`. `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s\n`reapDetachedRuns` recovers that run once the `detachedRunTtlMs` the\napplication passes to that sweep has elapsed — nothing derives it from\n`withSandbox`, which has no TTL option — so the cost is a delayed teardown\nrather than a lost one, provided the application actually schedules the\nsweep, which is its job and not the framework's. Still strictly better than\nfailing the teardown.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### runs\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n### runId\n\n`string`\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`boolean`\\>\n"}
